How the Program Works:
The Coffee Stack Visualizer is a Java program that demonstrates how a stack works using the LIFO (Last In, First Out) principle. 
When the program starts, the GUI displays the stack, its size, the top element, and the available buttons. When the user clicks a button, the GUI calls the appropriate method from the stack class. 
The stack is updated, and the GUI refreshes the display to show the current stack contents and status message.

